# The registered mark-caret1 plan (toolchain a0.0.47) rewrites every write
# mark `&` to `^` and every take mark `&&` to `^^` in an older-spelling
# source, a Markdown file and any other text: a parameter and a field type, a
# receiver and its footprint, a function type's parameter, a lambda's
# parameter, a call argument, a receiver mark at the start of a line, a
# window and an element window, a written match subject, a task capture, a
# shared type, a variadic pack, a mark after `&&` or `||`, a mark before an
# interpolated type in quoted Jet, a raw and a plain string's Jet, marks
# after a quoted line break, a code span in a string, a row's first
# parameter after its name in a triple-quoted string, a Jet `extern rust`
# block in a string though its link names hold `::`, a comment's code spans,
# a Jet fence, prose code spans and the source lines (after their gutter) and
# code spans of a diagnostic. The bit and logical operators (`a & b`, `a&b`,
# `ok &&done` in code and in a plain string, `&=`, `&~=`, comparisons joined
# with `&&`), HTML entities (`&amp;`, `&{name};`, `&...;`), a query string's
# `{s}&{piece}` and `&line={line}`, Rust's `&mut`, a string quoting C, Zig
# or COM (`goto `, a call ending `);`, `IID_`), a lowercase `[u8` slice, a
# code span after the word C, a YAML anchor whose alias the text names, a
# sign alone in a code span on a line about a separator, markup or the side
# of a logical `&&`, a run of three signs, other fences and prose outside
# code spans stay as written.
# A second run finds nothing left to rewrite.
fixture: MarkCaret1RewritesEveryMark/Input
step: jet run {root}/Compiler/Migrations/Migrate.jet -- mark-caret1 --write before.jet guide.md notes.txt
exit: 0
stdout: = "EDIT before.jet 39\nEDIT guide.md 6\nEDIT notes.txt 5\nTOTAL 50 sites in 3 files\n"
file: before.jet = MarkCaret1RewritesEveryMark/before.out
file: guide.md = MarkCaret1RewritesEveryMark/guide.out
file: notes.txt = MarkCaret1RewritesEveryMark/notes.out
step: jet run {root}/Compiler/Migrations/Migrate.jet -- mark-caret1 --write before.jet guide.md notes.txt
exit: 0
stdout: = "TOTAL 0 sites in 0 files\n"
file: before.jet = MarkCaret1RewritesEveryMark/before.out
file: guide.md = MarkCaret1RewritesEveryMark/guide.out
file: notes.txt = MarkCaret1RewritesEveryMark/notes.out
